                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "59589122",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197969421611",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 60,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 60,
                            "last_played": 1575947831
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I want to love this game, it's exactly what I was looking for. But it's half baked and does not deliver on it's promises. It should still be in early access, this is not something I would considered \"released\". It's like they gave up 60% of the way through development and said \"might as well release it, we're not going to finish it.\"\n\nMy main issues, since it's listed as released (would no consider these problems in a beta/early release scenario)\n- Literal messages that say \"insert_unit_message_here\"\n- Select all troops is finicky, only sometimes gets all troops or selects all and half ignore commands\n- When multiple troops selected and click to attack only half move or only one set of troops attack while 10+ sets just sit there being attacked and don't do anything\n- Lack of any real tutorial (more below)\n\nTutorial: it just says \"Build continuous troops and send them here\"  and how to do that... but with no details on how to handle resources to keep building troops. You can figure out how to do this, but you have to click around and figure out how to handle farms, upgrades, additional barracks, etc... all on your own as you're being attacked.\n\nThis was only from the first mission. I've put in to have the game refunded as I can't justify the cost in this state of \"released\". I assume the Devs are done with this and have no plans to fix these issues or improve this game if it was delivered in this state.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1575948958,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1575948958,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 33,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7206863164901733,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hello TheFynx.\nWe're sorry that you had difficulty with the tutorial in the game.\n\nWe did not want to overload the player with an abundance of information in the beginning of campaign. Therefore, the first mission of the campaign contains only basic information about the recruitment of troops.\nAlready in the second mission you will be told more about the collection of resources and the construction of buildings.\n\nIf you want to get complete information on the mechanics of the game, you can just select the \"Confrontation\" mode with the \"Beginner\" difficulty. There you will be described step by step the process of resource management, construction, recruitment and study technologies.\nWe hope you still play the game and be able to evaluate the learning system.  ",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1576010406,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
